# Shared DSPy rules (cursor-packs)

When creating or wiring dspy-go modules / interceptors / Create* XML:

- Load `.cursor/skills/dspy-module-patterns/SKILL.md`.

When writing or revising module prompts, signatures, or field descriptions:

- Load `.cursor/skills/dspy-prompt-engineering/SKILL.md` and its `reference.md` when depth is needed.
- Also load project `pipelines-x-*` prompt overlays if present.

When validation fails, fields look full in logs but parse empty, retries exhaust, or a refinement loop exits early:

- Load `.cursor/skills/dspy-go-debugging/SKILL.md`.
- Load `.cursor/skills/dspy-xml-structured-output/SKILL.md` for parser details.

Pipeline job layout (JobRunner, per-job clients): load `.cursor/skills/strop-pipeline-pattern/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/rules/strop.mdc` when orchestration or review is involved. Project overlays (if any) extend — do not replace — the pack pattern.
